{0 Extract Module Reference}


Monadic/applicative extractors for decoding [Record.t] (see ocaml/src/extract.mli).

Core
- ['a t] — extractor type
- Monad/Functor/App: [return], [fail], [bind] ([let*]), [let+], [and+]

Field extractors
- [field key decoder] where decoder is a [Record.at_*]
- Shortcuts: [text, int, int_as_int, bool, float, bytes, node, relationship, unbound_relationship, path, point2d, point3d, duration, date, local_time, time, local_datetime, datetime_zone_id, datetime_offset, value]
- Collections/maps: [list key element_exact], [map_field]

Optional
- [optional e] → ['a option t] (None when key missing)
- [default v e], [maybe key maybe_at_*], [maybe_text/int/bool/float/node/relationship/path]

Combinators
- [both], [sequence], [all]

Execution
- [run : 'a t -> Record.t -> ('a, Record.decode_error) result]
- [run_exn : 'a t -> Record.t -> 'a]

Composite helpers
- [pair], [triple], [text_int], [text_list], [int_list]
- Node: [node_props], [node_labels], [node_id]
- Relationship: [rel_type], [rel_props], [rel_id]
